{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_atouecv4sgl5k7g2iuprvtsuv74ly7iwhqysnxgbtcdin53eibnq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src/` is a single 645-line translation unit (a cute_c2-derived 2D collision library): vector/rotation/transform math, a GJK distance solver with simplex sub-solvers and index caching, boolean circle/AABB/capsule tests, and the `omni_collide` entry point declared in `include/lib.h`.\n\n## Deliverables\n- `Cargo.toml` — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`\n- `src/lib.rs` — 948 lines, all 39 functions, `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"`, no warnings\n\n## Completion gate — symbol diff is empty\n```\nC exports: 39   Rust exports: 39\nin C but MISSING from Rust: (none)\nin Rust but not in C:       (none)     DIFF EMPTY? YES\n```\n\n## Fidelity work beyond compiling\n- **ABI/layout**: verified every struct against gcc (`c2v` 8, `c2x` 16, `c2Capsule` 20, `c2GJKCache` 36, `c2Proxy` 72, `c2sv` 36, `c2Simplex` 152 with `b@36 c@72 d@108 div@144 count@148`) and locked them in with `const{assert!}`. `c2Simplex` uses `[c2sv;4]` so the C trick `c2sv *verts = &s.a; verts[i]` works identically; `c2GJK` uses raw pointer arithmetic exactly where C indexes unchecked.\n- **Bugs preserved, not fixed**: the inverted cache-validation condition (`&& metric < -1.0e8f`), `c2GJKSimplexMetric`'s `default:` falling into `case 1`, `ptr_from_parts`'s missing return on unknown type, `c2MakeProxy` leaving the proxy untouched for unknown types, and the exact order of every branch/error check.\n- **NaN-payload exactness**: `addss`/`mulss` return the *destination* operand when both operands are NaN, so operand order is observable. LLVM commuted several products/sums that gcc did not, so I disassembled the reference build, decoded the destination register per expression, and pinned each with ordered SSE helpers (x86_64 `asm!`, portable fallback) — e.g. `c2Dot` = `mulss dst=a.x`, `mulss dst=b.y`, `addss dst=` the second term; `den * u` in `c2Witness`/`c2L` has `dst=u`.\n\n## Verification (differential harness, both libs `dlopen`ed, results compared byte-wise)\n| Test | Result |\n|---|---|\n| All 39 symbols, 15.8M checks (incl. ±NaN, SNaN, NaN payloads, ±Inf, ±0) vs C | **0 failures** |\n| `c2GJK` full outputs (dist/outA/outB/iterations/cache), 5.4M calls, finite **and** NaN/Inf | **0 failures** |\n| Deterministic 36,864-case `omni_collide` grid | **byte-identical output** |\n| Symbol coverage | 39/39 exercised |\n\nTwo caveats worth stating plainly:\n1. I used gcc **`-O0`** as the reference, which is what both `cmake` (no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` in `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`) and a plain glob `gcc -shared -fPIC` produce. The C library is not self-consistent here: its own `-O2` build differs from its `-O0` build on **68,534** of those same checks, so no single translation can match both. My crate matches `-O0` exactly; against `-O2` the residual diffs are only NaN sign/payload bits, which cannot change any `int`/boolean result — the public `omni_collide` is identical to *both* builds on every input tested.\n2. Feeding `c2GJK` a cache whose `iA`/`iB` exceed the proxy's vertex count reads uninitialized stack in C (the two C builds disagree with each other by ~1.4M cases there). I zero-initialize for determinism; with in-range indices the match is exact.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified (md5s unchanged, 0 files touched)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1372,"cache_read_input_tokens":133263,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1372,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38ca38de-9922-4985-a85b-3fb69a9546dd","uuid":"d3702aca-4428-413c-ba2e-af36a3c89909","timestamp":"2026-08-20T03:48:52.155Z"}
